],"exit_code":0,"match_count":12,"file_matches":[{"path":"/Users/kimhawk/.local/state/h-mad/grok-audit-surface/run-ab2c85dc2e25-20261024T132452Z/roots/gas-root-d5-s2v1-e2mfcq1d/docs/02-design/features/tdd-gate-fail-opens.design.md","matches":[{"line_number":391,"content":"is owed to the operator; this revision does not change the hook. Codex parity for this case is covered under §\"Codex call"},{"line_number":463,"content":"Parity with the Claude root-refuse is not met on the tree, and this design does not close the"},{"line_number":480,"content":"Whether the Codex gate should refuse the mode-`000` member is owed to the operator (spec and"},{"line_number":709,"content":"| `M-18 M-14` | codex | step3 |"},{"line_number":820,"content":"- `M-18 M-14`, Codex gate, `step3` (operator decision 2026-09-30, spec v1.5; `step3` is"},{"line_number":867,"content":"| `_tree_b` identity stub; Claude `judge-timeout` rows; connection rows | `h-mad/tests/test_h_mad_tdd_gate_judge.py` | modify |"},{"line_number":917,"content":"  mapped to `judge-error` only when governed. They do not propagate to `# M:G2`. A payload-cwd"},{"line_number":935,"content":"| T1 | new module: `canonical_directory`, `canonicalise`, `fold_py_suffix`, `emit_canon`. The leaf scan follows a symlink leaf to the referent's parent and excludes symlink entries. `os.fsdecode` and `os.fsencode` are the filesystem codecs. The non-UTF-8 function test, the newline round-trip, and the AC-1.7 `os.path.realpath` substitution land in `h-mad/tests/test_h_mad_target_identity.py` |"},{"line_number":1134,"content":"AC-6.1 says: \"the differential passes on the fixed tree. On the unfixed tree its gate-equality"},{"line_number":1326,"content":"- v1.3: Operator decision (2026-09-30), sourced from spec v1.5: the Codex-gate key M-18 M-14 under step3 joins the approved deny-to-allow set as its seventh row (unfixed reading decision=deny kind=judge-error, fixed decision=allow kind=-). The approved table, the Verdicts that move toward ALLOW list, the T9 comparator expectation (COMPARE: PASS softened=7 approved=7) and the Guard narrowing count move from six to seven. Nothing else changes."},{"line_number":1327,"content":"- v1.4: Corrective revision, not re-audited (2026-09-30), from the operator decision after 6a-prime cycles 1 and 3 (docs/03-analysis/tdd-gate-fail-opens.archreview.v1.md, .v3.md). The Claude root-open rule is narrowed: the governed-only rule, including an ungoverned allow, applies only when the root can be entered and its state read (mode 0311). An absent, non-directory or non-enterable root is refused judge-error 'project root (CLAUDE_PROJECT_DIR) cannot be entered' before _chain_may_hold_state, pinned by h-mad/tests/test_h_mad_tdd_gate_judge.py::test_unenterable_project_dir_refuses (absent-root member only). Codex parity on the mode-000 member is recorded as NOT met on the tree (rglob swallows EACCES, status inactive, allow) and owed to the operator."},{"line_number":1328,"content":"- v1.5: Corrective revision, not re-audited (2026-09-30), from the operator decision after 6a-prime cycle 2 (docs/03-analysis/tdd-gate-fail-opens.archreview.v2.md, single-source contract), landed in d06d82f6, answering 6a-prime cycle 4 finding #3 (docs/03-analysis/tdd-gate-fail-opens.archreview.v4.md). The arm-2 component is the failing component in its on-disk spelling as resolved by the canonicaliser's _on_disk_component (sorted-first non-symlink same-inode name in its parent; spelled component when that lookup raises OSError); arm 1 stays spelled; both gates use it as-is with no gate-side re-derivation. For a root failure prefix and root stay the spelled root and component is its on-disk spelling. Pinned by h-mad/tests/test_h_mad_target_identity.py::test_unresolvable_component_is_reported_in_on_disk_spelling and ::test_unreadable_directory_is_arm_2[a-absent-leaf]. New conjunct residual: the Claude root-refuse CANON_COMPONENT=CANON_ROOT test is false for an existing mis-cased root, o [... truncated (1031 chars total)]"}]}]},"locations":[]}
{"type":"thought","data":"Checking lines 820, "}
{"type":"thought","data":"1044, and T2, plus Claude's"}
{"type":"thought","data":" note around 380-395"}
{"type":"thought","data":" about hook changes,"}
{"type":"thought","data":" to decide whether to"}
{"type":"thought","data":" include it."}
{"type":"thought","data":"\n\nDesign lines 120-140"}
{"type":"thought","data":" and T2 row near line"}
{"type":"thought","data":" 936 are being reviewed"}
{"type":"thought","data":" to quote the canonicalise"}
{"type":"thought","data":" walk description for"}
{"type":"thought","data":" N-1. The report is "}
{"type":"thought","data":"taking shape. A potential"}
{"type":"thought","data":" hard gap has been identified:"}
{"type":"thought","data":" the specification requires"}
{"type":"thought","data":" dropping `.` and not"}
{"type":"thought","data":" opening lexical `..`,"}
{"type":"thought","data":" but the algorithm section"}
{"type":"thought","data":" never states this rule,"}
{"type":"thought","data":" and T1 omits the relevant"}
{"type":"thought","data":" tests."}
{"type":"thought","data":"\n\nThe design omits the"}
{"type":"thought","data":" `.` and `..` rules "}
{"type":"thought","data":"entirely. The specification"}
{"type":"thought","data":" requires them. This"}
{"type":"thought","data":" is a must-fix because"}
{"type":"thought","data":" the design claims to"}
{"type":"thought","data":" decide which components"}
{"type":"thought","data":" are opened, yet the"}
{"type":"thought","data":" known fail-open case"}
{"type":"thought","data":" only appears in the"}
{"type":"thought","data":" changelog."}
{"type":"thought","data":"\n\nDesign line 190 is"}
{"type":"thought","data":" being quoted to show"}
{"type":"thought","data":" that intermediate ancestors"}
{"type":"thought","data":" are not opened, though"}
{"type":"thought","data":" this still does not"}
{"type":"thought","data":" resolve the `.` and"}
{"type":"thought","data":" `..` interaction.\n\n"}
{"type":"thought","data":"The T8 and test plan"}
{"type":"thought","data":" omissions of the v1.6"}
{"type":"thought","data":" pins will be folded"}
{"type":"thought","data":" into the same findings."}
{"type":"thought","data":"\n\nFor M-18, the design"}
{"type":"thought","data":" verdicts at line 820"}
{"type":"thought","data":" say the unfixed Codex"}
{"type":"thought","data":" gate denied the loop."}
{"type":"thought","data":" The test plan says "}
{"type":"thought","data":"both allow fixed and"}
{"type":"thought","data":" unfixed. AC-6.1 paraphrases"}
{"type":"thought","data":" stop before the spec's"}
{"type":"thought","data":" D-4 sentence. T6 refers"}
{"type":"thought","data":" to \"both failure sets\""}
{"type":"thought","data":" using incomplete sets.\n\nThe design verdicts"}
{"type":"thought","data":" section aligns with"}
{"type":"thought","data":" the specification, "}
{"type":"thought","data":"but the test plan contradicts"}
{"type":"thought","data":" both. This makes the"}
{"type":"thought","data":" unfixed differential"}
{"type":"thought","data":" check incorrect. Design"}
{"type":"thought","data":" test strategy line "}
{"type":"thought","data":"1066 expects fixed gates"}
{"type":"thought","data":" to deny judge-error"}
{"type":"thought","data":" under the governing"}
{"type":"thought","data":" state and allow under"}
{"type":"thought","data":" step3, yet the test"}
{"type":"thought","data":" plan row explicitly"}
{"type":"thought","data":" includes unfixed gates."}
{"type":"thought","data":" The `_tree_b` finding"}
{"type":"thought","data":" will be classified "}
{"type":"thought","data":"as Should-fix because"}
{"type":"thought","data":" the components table"}
{"type":"thought","data":" already contains the"}
{"type":"thought","data":" correct path."}
{"type":"thought","data":"\n\nThe fixtures section"}
{"type":"thought","data":" references a nonexistent"}
{"type":"thought","data":" file. The correct path"}
{"type":"thought","data":" is already present "}
{"type":"thought","data":"in the components table"}
{"type":"thought","data":" within the same document."}
{"type":"thought","data":" This is a Should-fix"}
{"type":"thought","data":" because an implementer"}
{"type":"thought","data":" following the prose"}
{"type":"thought","data":" would examine the wrong"}
{"type":"thought","data":" file, though the tests"}
{"type":"thought","data":" themselves would not"}
{"type":"thought","data":" change."}
{"type":"thought","data":"\n\nThe `_tree_b` finding"}
{"type":"thought","data":" is being upgraded to"}
{"type":"thought","data":" Must-fix. The wrong"}
{"type":"thought","data":" path in the fixtures"}
{"type":"thought","data":" section would misdirect"}
{"type":"thought","data":" a future implementer,"}
{"type":"thought","data":" since the design specifies"}
{"type":"thought","data":" where to edit the existing"}
{"type":"thought","data":" stub."}
{"type":"thought","data":"\n\nThe `_tree_b` finding is being downgraded to Should-fix. The components table already names the correct file, so the wrong path in the fixtures section is not a hard gate if both are read.\n\nA nit may be raised about history sections written in present tense without an end marker. This could instead belong to Must-fix 1.\n\nA new Should-fix finding has been identified: the Claude section at line 391, marked as superseded history, still claims the conjunct stays and the hook is unchanged. The live rule above drops the conjunct, creating a similar shape to the Codex history discrepancy."}
